@webref/css 8.7.5 (https://github.com/w3c/webref, npm package @webref/css), MIT licence
(LICENSE): the W3C's consolidation of the CSS features defined across the specifications,
scraped from the specifications themselves -- properties, types, functions, at-rules and their
descriptors, selectors, each with its value grammar ("Value Definition Syntax").

Onyx keeps only what libcss's grammar generator reads: css-grammar.json, made from the
package's css.json by trim.py (names and syntaxes). The generator,
third_party/libcss/src/parse/onyx_grammar_gen.py, compiles it into
third_party/libcss/src/parse/onyx_grammar_tables.c (committed: no Python at build time):

    npm pack @webref/css@8.7.5 && tar xzf webref-css-8.7.5.tgz
    python3 trim.py package/css.json > css-grammar.json
    cd ../libcss/src/parse && python3 onyx_grammar_gen.py \
        ../../../webref-css-8.7.5/css-grammar.json > onyx_grammar_tables.c

See docs/06-JET-BROWSER.md (CSS) for what libcss does with the grammars.
